{"name":"Sirocco","hex":"#68766e","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sirocco","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hot and often strong southerly to southeasterly wind on the Mediterranean that originates in the Sahara and adjacent North African regions.","A draft of hot air from an artificial source of heat."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sirocco"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sirocco","blocks":[{"text":"Sirocco or scirocco is a Mediterranean wind that comes from the Sahara and can reach hurricane speeds in North Africa and Southern Europe, especially during the summer season."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Brosen_windrose.svg/330px-Brosen_windrose.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sirocco","wikidata":"Q180372"},{"title":"Sirocco (parrot)","blocks":[{"text":"Sirocco is a kākāpō, a large, flightless, nocturnal parrot, and one of the remaining living individuals numbering only 325. He achieved individual fame following an incident on the BBC television series Last Chance to See in which he attempted to mate with zoologist Mark Carwardine. Subsequent featuring of the incident on television channels around the world and on YouTube resulted in Sirocco becoming internationally known. In his home country of New Zealand, Sirocco has attracted thousands of people during \"personal\" appearances, and in January 2010 was given the title of Official Spokesbird for Conservation by Prime Minister John Key. In this role, Sirocco helps advocate for conservation through human intermediaries on social media sites and blogs."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Sirocco_through_the_window.jpg/330px-Sirocco_through_the_window.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sirocco_(parrot)","wikidata":"Q7530532"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Sirocco_wind1.jpg/500px-Sirocco_wind1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Sirocco_wind1.jpg/500px-Sirocco_wind1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sirocco wind","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASirocco_wind1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Sahara_dust_Vitrolles.jpg/500px-Sahara_dust_Vitrolles.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Sahara_dust_Vitrolles.jpg/1280px-Sahara_dust_Vitrolles.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Sahara_dust_Vitrolles.jpg/500px-Sahara_dust_Vitrolles.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Effects of sirocco: Saharan dust in Vitrolles, France.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASahara_dust_Vitrolles.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Sirocco_at_the_door.jpg/330px-Sirocco_at_the_door.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Sirocco_at_the_door.jpg/330px-Sirocco_at_the_door.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sirocco guards the hut during the 2008 breeding season.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASirocco_at_the_door.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/92/Party_Parrot.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/92/Party_Parrot.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt